        # used to mark a symbol's shares as "gone" the instant the sell
        # order was SUBMITTED, not once IB actually confirmed it filled.
        # If that order is ever rejected or just never executes (the most
        # common real-world cause: a plain MKT order submitted outside
        # regular trading hours, which IB generally won't run until the
        # next session), the broker would still show real shares held
        # while this engine believed they were already sold, with
        # nothing to retry it. This matters MORE now that bare share
        # positions (see the reconciliation-loop fix in positionEnd())
        # also route through this same liquidation path — a silently
        # failed sell order there would leave the symbol permanently
        # stuck in limbo rather than genuinely freed up. These two sets
        # fix that:
        #   liquidation_needed_symbols: symbols THIS ENGINE has decided
        #     need to be fully sold off (added the first time
        #     trigger_liquidate_shares() is ever called for that symbol),
        #     kept until the broker confirms zero shares remain.
        #   liquidation_pending_symbols: symbols with a liquidation order
        #     CURRENTLY working, so the sweep doesn't pile up duplicate
        #     sell orders while one is still in flight.
        # See sweep_orphaned_shares(), called at the end of every
        # positionEnd() pass using that pass's live broker share count.
        self.liquidation_needed_symbols = set()
        self.liquidation_pending_symbols = set()
 
